From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 04:49:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07267/11362] [outer-loop] document conductor stale-import
 gotcha (fixed lint, stale process)

The conductor kept refusing milestone .511's activation on the arc-levelup-guarantee
check for hours after the lint script itself was already fixed to self-retire
(commit 56d91abec, 2026-07-17). Root cause: research_conductor.py imports
arc_levelup_guarantee_lint via a plain `from X import Y` inside its activation-guard
function; Python caches that module on first import and never re-reads it from disk,
so the long-lived conductor process (alive since 2026-07-13) kept calling the
pre-retirement version of lint_roadmap() even though the file on disk -- and every
fresh subprocess invocation -- had the fix the whole time. No code fix needed: a
conductor restart forces a fresh import and picks up the already-correct file.
Documented so a future session doesn't waste time re-testing the lint file instead
of recognizing the conductor process itself needs restarting.

